WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.355 --> 00:00:06.200
Guayarmina and the Tibicena of the Ravine

2
00:00:06.775 --> 00:00:11.980
In ancient Gran Canaria, Guayarmina led a
small herd along a path through a ravine.

3
00:00:12.575 --> 00:00:18.140
As the sun set, she gathered the goats
beside a cave and lit a torch.

4
00:00:18.795 --> 00:00:21.360
Suddenly, she heard a growl.

5
00:00:21.775 --> 00:00:25.860
A figure covered in black fur appeared
among the tabaibas.

6
00:00:26.275 --> 00:00:31.540
It had the shape of a large dog, and its
eyes looked like two glowing embers.

7
00:00:32.135 --> 00:00:36.895
Guayarmina remembered the stories of the
tibicenas, beings who wandered through

8
00:00:36.895 --> 00:00:38.460
caves and lonely places.

9
00:00:39.575 --> 00:00:44.560
Fear urged her to run, but she called to
the other goatherds.

10
00:00:44.995 --> 00:00:50.075
Together they raised their torches and
said: “Together in the light, fear grows

11
00:00:50.075 --> 00:00:51.075
small.”

12
00:00:51.455 --> 00:00:53.660
The tibicena circled the fire once.

13
00:00:54.155 --> 00:00:55.680
Then it went round again.

14
00:00:56.155 --> 00:00:59.575
The third time round, it stopped in front
of Guayarmina.

15
00:00:59.575 --> 00:01:04.340
She asked Acorán for protection and stayed
beside the herd.

16
00:01:04.975 --> 00:01:10.195
When the sky began to grow light, the
creature backed away until it disappeared

17
00:01:10.195 --> 00:01:11.260
among the rocks.

18
00:01:12.075 --> 00:01:16.260
Large footprints remained on the ground,
mixed with the tracks of goats.

19
00:01:16.915 --> 00:01:20.220
Guayarmina told the people of the village
what had happened.

20
00:01:20.715 --> 00:01:25.915
The elders could not say for certain what
she had seen, but they were thankful that

21
00:01:25.915 --> 00:01:28.700
no one had ventured into the ravine alone.

22
00:01:29.855 --> 00:01:36.355
From then on, whenever night caught the
goatherds by surprise, they gathered the

23
00:01:36.355 --> 00:01:43.060
herd, lit the torch and remembered:
“Together in the light, fear grows small.”

